-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture/journal repairs, supersampling, capture safeguards and faithful diagnostics. Retain ordered scene initialization, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor comparisons. This quality correction introduces no additional presentation repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- First verify import ordering and formatting in the two affected modules, then run the repository quality-debt gate without changing its baselines.\n- Run both existing modules across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Retain combining-mark, wide-cell, clipping, trailing-cell, color/style, unavailable-evidence and non-mutation controls, plus production tab-focus restoration coverage. Formatting alone needs no new tests.\n- Run adjacent ruler-trace, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret and completion coverage.\n- Require fresh final-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Obtain trusted isolated candidate captures at **208×47 cells** and **1280×800 pixels**. Require all **46 geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts**, including reassessment of ruler, caret and new-file findings. Preserve picker comparisons and first-failure diagnostics.\n- Bind checks and artifacts to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Inconclusive findings remain unresolved; demonstrated further repairs require renewed independent planning.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding, then complete independent feature/source and visual review. Review every diff continuation and companion implementation; retrieved pages alone do not establish assessed coverage.\n- Preserve current-dev safeguards, authenticated history, credentials, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery and exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete that broader objective.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."},{"answer_index":24,"id":"b239df38a3cbbd33de3627b25a36e9063e036dac68b6e9c97c83d69c701c88f3","text":"1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions."},{"answer_index":25,"id":"ba800d0ea428ec7a001c0765a90362402cdfe85aa29ac8ae5d7e49a96975ad4b","text":"1. Should the plan restore the newly pinned dev’s capture/export safeguards before completing the outstanding independent review? The current diff deletes `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`, its regression module and a parent-objective record, reverts `agent-visual.yml`, and removes failed-capture documentation.\nPreserve dev safeguards (Recommended): Restore those files and workflow exactly from pinned dev, retain its documentation plus the feature-specific activation section, preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch, then obtain fresh review and GitHub validation.\nReview before reconciliation: Complete read-only assessment of the published predecessor first; keep current-base reconciliation and final candidate validation blocked until separately planned."},{"answer_index":26,"id":"7955d1db22074defa82b9d57196aac7ba36a0679d4226fe9ad241de670ff3d1e","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the inherited column ruler and route the reported stray “1” for independent reassessment, using the inspected PNG, separate ruler/editor geometry, identical pinned-dev ruler source, and existing empty-document assertion? This resolves the correction approach only; the rejecting visual gate remains in force until independently reviewed.\nPreserve ruler (Recommended): Preserve production presentation; add a focused tab-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene evidence, then repeat independent full-feature and visual review.\nChange ruler presentation: Authorize a narrow presentation change to distinguish column labels from gutter numbers; its exact appearance needs a further decision before implementation."},{"answer_index":27,"id":"46377a331dc01c2e34cff52b83d9ddd5e5dd1b98a41de0000d6832f0d20a0a45","text":"1. Should the renewed plan first collect bounded, GitHub-only evidence for the indistinct secondary carets before choosing a production or export repair? The inspected PNG confirms the visibility finding, but its geometry does not identify the failing layer.\nDiagnose first (Recommended): Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work; add exact cursor/focus/scroll state, caret-cell widget/compositor styles and lossless SVG evidence with focused regressions, then independently plan the demonstrated repair after GitHub capture.\nChange caret presentation: Plan a production presentation change now; its precise appearance requires another choice and must preserve SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping."},{"answer_index":28,"id":"1533c21a5bce25f66a9d4d6d9395969fe2d15e25112b4e9000ea13507588cdd7","text":"1. May the renewed plan include narrow repairs for the newly verified journal-error status and new-file dialog alignment, after identifying their failing layers? These extend the earlier enumerated UI repair scope.\nNarrow gate repairs (Recommended): Show read failures without claiming empty results, restore intended dialog centering, add focused regressions, and retain the complete feature and all review gates.\n\n2. Should the correction fix the confirmed diagnostic/test defects and collect missing command-caret and ruler lifecycle evidence before selecting further presentation or focus changes?\nFaithful diagnostics (Recommended): Fix variable shadowing and lint, preserve combining marks and cell styles during cropping, retain strict assertions, and diagnose ruler focus/width and command-caret layers on GitHub without forcing scene state."},{"answer_index":29,"id":"310ef79ccea7f258fef9f5fee47aebad16404f96b3ab0e5fc0e03fac1fad6e90","text":"1. Which correction sequence should the renewed plan specify for the observed ruler focus and row-width failures? Existing assertions and production ruler presentation must remain intact.\nTrace lifecycle (Recommended): Fix the confirmed lint/format findings, preserve current-dev safeguards, and add bounded GitHub-only callback-order and strip-padding observations before selecting the focus or width correction.\nCorrect scene lifecycle: Plan command focus after tab restoration and full-width widget-row collection now; retain strict equality and negative controls, then require GitHub reproduction and independent review."},{"answer_index":30,"id":"fd123ca6bb2e97c0179d0650913397f70c39425e6f71229ff3f98ad248a446a7","text":"1. Should the renewed plan correct the demonstrated harness-layer mismatch: apply the scene’s intended command focus after deferred tab restoration, and compare Textual’s styled widget rows with compositor rows while retaining the original unpadded strips as separate evidence? Production tab behavior and ruler presentation would stay unchanged; strict equality, negative controls, and all feature/review gates remain required.\nCorrect harness layers (Recommended): Use ordered scene initialization and native styled-row collection, preserve raw observations, fix confirmed lint/format findings, and validate on GitHub.\nExtend diagnostics first: Preserve the failing harness and collect native styled-row and focus-application traces on GitHub before separately planning its correction."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}